<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Allah ibn Qasim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn Qasim was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpuente">Alpuente</a> in the Valencian uplands, ruling from the fortress town of Alpuente in the early 11th century after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He took the honorific title Yumn al-Dawla. His family, the Banu Qasim, kept the small principality of castles and valleys until the Almoravid conquest in the early 12th century.</p></div>
